ECS: and EKS are container orchestration services.
Fargate: is a serverless compute engine that can be used as a launch type for both ECS tasks and EKS pods,
abstracting away the underlying server infrastructure. This allows you to run containers without managing
servers, simplifying operations and potentially optimizing costs.
If not fargate then cluster runs on EC2s.

Cluster - master and nodes, nodes run the actual workload.
Pod - one or more containers (usually one). 
Controller
Service

